      "writtenOn": "2025-07-18T14:15:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Good point. The logic here seems correct, but a bit redundant, and the name `pgt_switched` a bit misleading (pgt switching is per CPU, whereas this variable check is used rather for the global state \"host EPT allocated, and EPT address translation enabled on at least one CPU\").\n\nEssentially `pgt_switched` duplicates  the `static bool pkvm_init` variable? So we can just move that `pkvm_init` variable to the global scope (and rename it to some more suitable name)?",
      "parentUuid": "e6dbb0fb_c7643b49",
      "revId": "08f1b0eeab64a890f0819adf3a3b153513fe0a4f",
